# operator_overload_compose.tkr — the §9A ACCEPT host: method AND operator overload resolved ACROSS
# composition (the Overload branch of the AST-equality merge). Each scenario names itself and asserts
# its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself. A distinct-signature
# same-name member from a composed trait coexists with the host's own on the flattened surface, and
# `select_overload` picks at the call site.

Feature: operator_overload_compose — method/operator overload across composition (§9A Overload branch)

  Scenario: method_overload_compose — Host.k(i32) via the trait, Host.k(str) via the host, picked by select_overload
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario method_overload_compose: ok"

  Scenario: operator_overload_compose — Box + i32 and Box + Box select distinct composed __add legs
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario operator_overload_compose: ok"
